		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4211&amp;p=32001#p32001"><![CDATA[
I converted my MD-9600 to opengd77 today.<br><br>Used a V5 firmware , and the 20240621 CPS.<br>Quite sure Original FW+CPS said HW V2.xx<br><br>The Radio Info after conversion now says it's a V5.<br>Is that determined by me uploading a V5 firmware or some real hw trickery on the specific model ???<br><br><br>Backed up the "Original fw" CPS + Cal-data (CTL-T)<br><strong class="text-strong">Loaded opengd77.</strong><br>Backed up the Flash + Registers + MCU-Flash<br>Backed up Cal-Data again (opengd77)<br><br>Loaded the Sweden CPS from here  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_cool.gif" width="15" height="17" alt="8-)" title="Cool"> <br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=14&amp;t=3973" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=14&amp;t=3973</a><br><br>Loaded the full DMR-ID database ... Took some time.<br><br><br><strong class="text-strong">Thank you team</strong>  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"> <br><br>There's a bit Radio Dead in the summerhouse (Sweden near Laholm)<br>Or maybe I just don't know what channels they use around here.<br><br>So i have just tested w. my DM-1701's ....<br><br>My VHF/UHF antenna (1.6mtr GP) is <strong class="text-strong">inside</strong> at the moment, but in my summer vacation i'll mount it on a side-arm at the TV antenna mast tube.<br><br>I ordered a MD-9600 w GPS , but OpenGD77 says <strong class="text-strong">NO GPS Found</strong><br>Do I need to enable the GPS in a setting, saw some mumbling about a FET controlling the power in the RT3 mod.<br>But the guide, kinda hint that the GPS on a MD-9600 cant be set to Off ... So maybe there's no GPS power control in that one ??<br><br>Or does the NO GPS Found on a MD-9600 indicate there is just no GPS in it ??<br><br>.<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2496&amp;sid=2d2cd6ed8ef1469eecbb9bc35d4f34a6" class="postimage" alt="md-9600-gps.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>.<br><br>I'ts not a biggie, I think GPS was an extra 6$, and i actually have a few of the "mini GPS'es" w antenna, lying around.<br>The one used in the RT3 mods around here.<br><br>I could also just extend the serial + pwr wires out the back as Roger did , and use an external gps or nmea stream.<br>I have actually been thinking about making a RS-485 "shack net", and feed it from the LEA-M8T, already in my DIY STM32F407 NTP server.<br>Since i have a lot of devices wanting gps (nmea) info, and my 4-port gps-antenna splitter is already full.<br><br>.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5917">OZ1FTG</a> — Sat Jul 06, 2024 10:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
